<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Oct grain import value up 9.7 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Oct grain import value up 9.7 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The value of Taiwan's grain and oilseed imports in October rose 9.7 percent to US$255.6 million from $232.9 million in October 1995, the Finance Ministry said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Taiwan traders attributed the rise in grain import value mainly to the high international prices in October.</p>
<p>October's import tonnage figures were not available.</p>
<p>The following are import figures for major grain categories in millions of U.S. dollars:</p>
<p>			   October 1996    October 1995</p>
<p> Wheat			13.2		  20</p>
<p> Corn			 92.1		 100</p>
<p> Soybeans		   83.0		44.8</p>
<p>--Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
